= The Occupation of the Ruhr

On 11 January French and Belgian troops cross into the Ruhr with tanks and machine guns. Within a week sixty thousand soldiers guard the pits, the coking plants and the railway yards from Essen to Dortmund. Germany has fallen behind with its deliveries of coal and timber, and the French engineers have come to take the coal themselves.

[? if e22_workers_gov = 0 : Cuno proclaims passive resistance. No official is to obey the French, and the Reich will pay the wages of every man who stops work. The money will be printed. ?][? if e22_workers_gov > 0 : The workers' government calls for passive resistance and pays the strike wages with money from the presses. The mine owners join the resistance in public and sell their coal to France in private. ?][? if e23_red_ruhr = 1 : The councils that have run the Ruhr since 1920 face foreign bayonets, and the French have orders to disarm them. ?]

- @both: Fight Poincaré on the Ruhr and Cuno on the Spree.
- @seize: Take over the pits the owners have abandoned.
- @national: Join the national resistance.

@both
subtitle: The party stays between the two camps, and the Ruhr listens.
on-arrival: {!
RG.ecci('radek', 4);
RG.district('ruhr', {members: 0.05, loyalty: 4});
Q.e23_ruhr_line = 1;
Q.lean_unionist += 1;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 1;
!}

Our leaflets at the pit gates say the French soldiers are workers in uniform and the German owners are profiteers in mourning. Leaflets in French appear in the barracks of Essen the same week.

@seize
subtitle: [? if lock_councils = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] Pit committees dig coal for the miners' families. Both armies will answer.
choose-if: lock_councils < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids occupations.
on-arrival: {!
RG.e22.against('councils');
RG.startStrike('ruhr');
RG.district('ruhr', {guards: 2, repression: 8, loyalty: 6, members: 0.08});
RG.ecci('bukharin', 6);
RG.ecci('radek', -5);
Q.e23_ruhr_line = 3;
Q.lean_offensive += 2;
!}

In Gelsenkirchen, Bochum and Mülheim pit committees led by our members take over the mines the owners have left. They dig coal for the miners' families and for nobody else. The French commander and the German owners both call it anarchy.

@national
subtitle: [? if lock_moscow_orders = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] Radek's private advice. Some nationalists listen, and many of our own are disgusted.
on-arrival: {!
RG.e22.against('moscow_orders');
RG.ecci('radek', 6);
Q.e23_ruhr_line = 4;
Q.independence -= 5;
Q.unity -= 5;
Q.worker_support += 2;
!}

Our deputies vote for the emergency credits. In the Ruhr our members stand beside the Catholic priests at the funerals of the first strikers shot by the French.
